// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'binding'. Valid alternatives: ['database']
//
// `sink:` is Relational{database} XOR ObjectStorage{binding}. The two sub-rules are
// `(sinkDatabase)*` and `(sinkBinding)*` -- each accepts an EMPTY body, so which sink kind
// you wrote is decided entirely by the keyword and the field inside is unconstrained by it
// in every direction the grammar can express. What it CAN express is that `binding` is not
// one of the relational sink's fields, which is what this file writes.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::RelationalSinkWithBinding
{
  doc: 'relational sink given an object storage binding';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  persister: Batch
  {
    sink: Relational
    {
      binding: test::persistence::Binding;
    }
    ingestMode: NontemporalSnapshot
    {
      auditing: None;
    }
    targetShape: Flat
    {
      modelClass: test::persistence::ModelClass;
      targetName: 'TestDataset1';
    }
  }
}
